\section{The first cohort: DD1317 in autumn 2026}
\label{app:prgi26}

The instrument of \cref{app:diagnostics} first ran in DD1317, autumn
2026 (Canvas course prgi26).
It did not run as planned: the quizzes were ready only when the course
had taught four of its topics, and the course's teacher then arranged
them to fit the course as it stood.
This appendix records what the cohort did instead, for two readers.
The analysis of this cohort needs to know which measures exist and
what they mean; and the next course to run the instrument should run
it as planned (\cref{app:diagnostics-deployment}), which this record
shows the reason for.
It is also the cohort's deployment: tangled together with
\cref{app:diagnostics}, its chunks reproduce the quizzes as they stand
in Canvas.

\subsection{What ran, and where}

The Python part of the course started in week~37.
The quizzes were created in Canvas on 4--5 October 2026, at the end of
week~40, when the course had taught functions and variables,
conditionals, data types and repetitions and was about to teach
dictionaries and classes in week~41.
Three things follow from that date.
\begin{description}
\item[No course-level start quiz] The start of the course had passed,
  so the course-level start quiz was never deployed, and with it went
  the consent item that the other quizzes rely on.
\item[A catch-up module instead of four before-quizzes] The
  before-quizzes of the four taught topics, and of reading programs,
  which the course practises from the first week, could no longer run
  before their units.
  Their after-quizzes were collected in a module of their own,
  \enquote{Diagnostiskt prov: det du lärt dig hittills}, placed right
  before the classes week; the teacher decided to make it a
  prerequisite of that week's module, so every student takes stock of
  the course so far before continuing.
\item[Bracketing pairs for the rest] The remaining three topics ---
  classes and dictionaries (week~41), containers (week~44) and files
  (week~45) --- got their before- and after-quizzes.
  The containers before-quiz was later withdrawn (see below), so only
  classes and dictionaries and files kept both.
\end{description}

The teacher then changed the placement in Canvas, and the chunks below
follow those changes.
First, every quiz title got the suffix \enquote{(obligatorisk)}, as
every compulsory item in the course has; the analysis finds the quizzes
by searching for the planned title, so the suffix does not disturb it.
Second, the after-quiz of one unit and the before-quiz of the next were
moved out of the units' modules into a \emph{gateway} module between
the two, named \enquote{Diagnostiskt prov: inför \ldots} after the
unit that follows.
Third, on 23 October, three days before the containers unit, the
teacher withdrew the containers before-quiz, which had not yet been
published, and moved the containers after-quiz back to where the
planned deployment puts it, last in its unit's module.
The files after-quiz went to the revision module before the computer
exam, next to the course-level end quiz, which left the gateway module
\enquote{Diagnostiskt prov: inför projektet} empty.
The classes before-quiz and the containers after-quiz are thus the
only quizzes where the planned deployment puts them.
